  "question": "Do RTPS reliability control messages explain the late EGO pose-reader sequence holes observed in the depth A/B runs?",
  "decision": {
    "finding": "An EGO ACKNACK requests an exact missing writer sequence; a same-sequence DATA retransmission follows about 5.12 ms later, reaches the EGO receive API, then causes ordered Fast DDS DataReader delivery. In the second run, delayed retransmissions for 399 and 402 arrive at the EGO receive API only just after the next successful take, while DataReader history in the gap stops at 398.",
    "root_cause_boundary": "RTPS reliable-recovery/head-of-line delay is directly observed as the mechanism spanning the missing sequence and stale take interval. Why the first DATA copy was not returned by the EGO receive API remains unresolved; participant socket counters cannot assign the loss to those packet sequences.",
    "canonical_change": "none",
    "status": "P2 remains passed with health thresholds PROVISIONAL; GOAL C and overall A-H remain pending."
  },
